Step 3: Visualizing Results
The script produces two important plots:

3D Trajectory Plot: This shows a spiraling trajectory of the satellite heading toward Earth as it re-enters.
Altitude vs Time Plot: It shows the orbit is decaying continuously due to atmospheric drag, with greater acceleration coming from denser layers of atmosphere as the satellite descends.

Both plots provide insights into the process of deorbiting and a confidence check for simulation accuracy.
